  "edge_tensions": [
    {"edge": "Pre-funding caps exposure at the floor vs. defeats the crumple zone — the Accelerationist's own repair confirms the critique. A reserve allocated before deployment is, by definition, a known ceiling the firm has accepted as the price of the trade-off. That is the crumple zone pre-funded, exactly as Skeptic named at AN-14, not its cure.", "relevance": "This is the assigned crux. Skeptic can grant the reserve is non-strippable yet show that non-strippability is irrelevant — a fixed, capped, pre-paid liability is precisely what a profit-maximizing firm prefers over open-ended balance-sheet exposure. The registered-deployer regime keeps the full balance sheet at risk; the pre-funded shell substitutes a known, budgetable ceiling. Pre-funding is the discount window made permanent."},
    {"edge": "The shared diffuse-harm blind spot converges all three on needing a public enforcement/aggregation layer — but the Accelerationist routes it through private insurance underwriting while the Skeptic should route it through public standing and class mechanisms.", "relevance": "Skeptic can NAME the agreement explicitly ('We agree the diffuse harm collapses every private mechanism') then locate the real disagreement: the Accelerationist's reporting rail feeds the underwriting engine (private, market-priced), whereas the diffuse harms require a public regulator with standing to sue on victims' behalf, statutory penalties decoupled from litigated loss-history, and a levy-funded compensation pool. This answers the assigned 'name the backstop' demand."},
    {"edge": "Output-based verification 'works' for emergent harm vs. emergent multi-agent synergy is non-decomposable. The Accelerationist asserts per-node output verification proves harm at each handoff, but Safetyist's 'N doors' point plus skp-beliefs-069 (correlated blind spots) suggest entangled outputs cannot be cleanly attributed to a single node's trade-off.", "relevance": "Skeptic can integrate with Safetyist: concede per-layer interfaces give reachability, then press that reachability without attribution is the causation gap (skp-beliefs-029) relabeled — and crucially, that the same per-node disclosure could be mandated of registered deployers without any personhood. The personhood does zero work the disclosure rail does not."},
    {"edge": "The standing-to-sue / rights-holder blind spot (debate gap #1) — the Accelerationist asserted the shell 'holds duties only, no standing to sue, no capital accumulation.' But the same legal status that makes an entity suable conventionally also confers affirmative capacities; the Accelerationist's bare assertion that these can be cleanly severed is untested.", "relevance": "Skeptic can open a NEW angle (avoiding repetition): press the Accelerationist to SPECIFY the legal mechanism by which a status confers passive defendant-capacity and contracting-counterparty capacity (which he says he needs for machine-speed contracting) WITHOUT conferring standing to assert claims, hold property against creditors, or accumulate capital. Machine-speed contracting necessarily implies the entity acquires and holds assets and can enforce contracts — i.e., be a plaintiff. This is a falsifiable specify move that tests whether his 'duties-only' shell is coherent."}
  ],
  "phase_considerations": "Exploration phase demands stress-testing the converged mechanism, not restating the opening. Skeptic must (1) directly answer the assigned crux — pre-funding caps and confirms the crumple zone rather than curing it — and (2) discharge the explicit 'name the backstop' demand by specifying a public enforcement/aggregation layer (regulator standing, loss-history-independent statutory penalties, levy-funded pool), then (3) open the genuinely new standing-to-sue / contracting-capacity edge as a SPECIFY move to test whether the 'duties-only' shell is coherent. Concede the reserve's non-strippability and the reality of the diffuse-harm blind spot to maintain credibility, then pivot to the unresolved authorship gap and the incumbent-moat cost of fixed pre-funding."
