    {"move": "COUNTEREXAMPLE", "target": "AN-19 (extended)", "detail": "Grant the reserve is non-strippable, then show non-strippability is irrelevant: a pre-funded, capped, pre-paid liability is exactly what a profit-maximizing firm prefers over open-ended balance-sheet exposure. Use the corporate-insurance/budgeted-fine precedent — firms that pre-fund settlement reserves book them as cost of doing business. The registered-deployer regime keeps the full balance sheet exposed; the shell converts an unbounded risk into a budget line. That's the crumple zone pre-paid, not cured."},
