  "argument_sketch": "Open by granting the reserve's non-strippability and naming why that concession costs him nothing — a capped, pre-paid liability is the sociopath's preferred outcome, the discount window made permanent, which confirms the crumple zone I named earlier. Then discharge the backstop demand with a concrete public layer (regulator standing, loss-history-independent penalties, levy-funded pool) and explain why the diffuse harm forces it public, not private. Close by cracking the 'duties-only' shell open: demand he specify how machine-speed contracting can exist without the entity holding assets and enforcing contracts — and if it holds and enforces, it is a plaintiff and a property-holder, which is the liability shield I warned about, and which a registered deployer never needs.",
